| `agents.protected_paths.<path>` | string | twenty-one paths, each with its reason: the checks and gate scripts (`scripts`, `tests`, `evals`, `runtimes`, and `api/rest_fastapi/export_openapi.py`, which `make check-openapi` runs), the agents' own instructions (`agents`, `.claude`), the judge's configuration (`config`, `pyproject.toml` and its twin), the approved text (`CONVENTIONS.md`, `docs/adr`, `docs/specs`), the commit and CI gates, git's own state (`.git`), `models`, the copier files and the `.jinja` twins of `.gitignore` and `.copier-answers.yml`; `config` must stay covered or the policy is refused | a repo-relative POSIX path (no leading or trailing `/`, no empty, `.` or `..` part) mapped to a non-blank reason; at least one entry | `scripts/apply_refactor.py` (`load_policy`, `protected_by`) | Refuses, before any write, an agent edit to the named path and everything under it, judged on case-folded parts as written and after resolving symlinks. Beneath the map, an edit to a file git does not track (git's own state, an ignored file, `.venv`, `node_modules`, a new file) is refused whatever the map says. Removing an entry lets an edit there apply; a map that leaves `config/project.json` uncovered, an empty map or a blank reason is a config fault (exit 14). An entry for a path the tree lacks protects nothing and is not an error. | a direct interactive edit outside `scripts/apply_refactor.py`: hooks or permission rules, not built | always |
